                        <description>Time-evolving stream datasets exist ubiquitously in many real-world applications where their inherent hot keys often evolve over times. Nevertheless, few existing solutions can provide efficient load balance on these time-evolving datasets while preserving low memory overhead. In this paper, we present a novel grouping approach (named FISH), which can provide the efficient time-evolving stream processing at scale. The key insight of this work is that the keys of time-evolving stream data can hav</description> 
